; The construction layer (P8): build_providers / build_extractor /
; build_fetch_stack / build_app, kept out of the server's startup path so
; [--check] can diagnose a deployment without building the MCP server. It is its
; own library — [seekwright.factory], wrapped as [Seekwright_factory] — for the
; same reason [lib/providers/] is one: the adapters depend on [seekwright], so a
; factory inside that library could not name them without closing a cycle
; (plans/seekwright-ocaml-port.md, the P4 note).

(library
 (name seekwright_factory)
 (public_name seekwright.factory)
 ; The facade's signature is derived from [Providers_build], [Verdict],
 ; [Fetch_stack] and [App] by [include], so those four must stay nameable: a
 ; public signature that names a [private_modules] member installs a dangling
 ; path (plans/seekwright-ocaml-port.md §11, and the probe recorded in
 ; plans/factory-split-proposal.md §2.2). Naming them adds nothing to the
 ; surface — each of their interface names is already re-exported by [Factory].
 ; [grants] is the one seal: its [grant_of_decision] and
 ; [fs_grant_of_written_root] build a grant from a confinement decision, and a
 ; consumer that could reach them could build one outside the funnel. The seal
 ; keeps installed consumers and odoc away from it; a stanza inside this
 ; workspace can still reach it through dune's alias module, so the check-path
 ; boundary is pinned by source in [test/test_caps_audit.ml].
 (private_modules grants)
 (libraries
  seekwright
  seekwright.providers
  seekwright.fetch
  mcp-caps
  eio
  uri
  yojson))
